      "content": "I'll start by reading both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of the test. I'll write an improved version with better readability — clearer constants, descriptive variable names, and comments that explain the intent without changing behavior.Now I'll run the compile check.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version adds a descriptive class-level comment explaining the intent, named string constants (`firstPart`/`secondPart`) to make the input-output relationship explicit, per-assertion failure messages, and inline section comments marking the transition from the first reader to the second — all without changing any method calls, arguments, or expected outcomes."
